@startuml invoice-state-machine

' A42-11 — laid out left to right so the happy path DRAFT -> IN_REVIEW ->
' ISSUED reads as one line, entry at the left, both exits at the right. The
' IN_REVIEW -> DRAFT back-edge stays a short local return arrow between the
' two adjacent boxes (no direction hint on it: PlantUML/Graphviz drops one
' of a pair of same-rank edges that carry opposing -left-/-right- hints —
' verified against docker plantuml/plantuml:1.2023.12, the version `make
' publish` renders with).
' The storno document's [*] --> CANCELLED entry used to share the diagram's
' single real start pseudostate with [*] --> DRAFT, which pulled that dot
' into a crossing-heavy spot between the two flows. It is now its own
' <<start>>-stereotyped pseudostate (StornoEntry) placed right next to
' CANCELLED — same solid-dot look as a real start, but visually a distinct
' second entry, which is the point: a storno document is never created via
' DRAFT, it is born directly in CANCELLED. One shared <<end>> pseudostate
' (End) is the single exit for ISSUED (stays sent), CANCELLED and VOIDED —
' PO 2026-09-12: one exit, two confused readers.
'
' State colours follow the shared status chip tones (lifecycleTone in the UI; the
' same meaning carries the same colour in the offer diagram,
' quote-state-machine.puml). The real chips are pale-tint pills sized for 12px UI
' labels; for a diagram box the tone colour becomes a solid fill with white label
' text (FontSize 12 bold is "normal text", AA bar 4.5:1). Contrast against white:
'   DRAFT      NEUTRAL --lt-text-secondary #5F6368 = 6.05:1
'   IN_REVIEW  REVIEW  #C34118 (darkened --lt-review #F4511E) = 5.13:1
'   ISSUED       ACCENT  #1A73E8 = 4.51:1
'   CANCELLED  STORNO  #455A64 = 7.24:1
'   VOIDED     ERROR   #D93025 = 4.77:1
' Borders are a darker shade of the same hue; they are decoration and carry no
' AA requirement of their own.

left to right direction

skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 40

skinparam defaultFontName "Roboto, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam state {
  FontSize 12
  FontStyle bold
  FontColor #ffffff
  ArrowColor #5F6368
  ArrowFontColor #202124
  ArrowFontSize 11
}

skinparam state<<draft>> {
  BackgroundColor #5F6368
  BorderColor #4A4D51
}

skinparam state<<review>> {
  BackgroundColor #C34118
  BorderColor #9C3412
}

skinparam state<<sent>> {
  BackgroundColor #1A73E8
  BorderColor #145AB5
}

skinparam state<<cancelled>> {
  BackgroundColor #455A64
  BorderColor #36464E
}

skinparam state<<voided>> {
  BackgroundColor #D93025
  BorderColor #A9251D
}

state DRAFT <<draft>>
state IN_REVIEW <<review>>
state ISSUED <<sent>>
state CANCELLED <<cancelled>>
state VOIDED <<voided>>
state "  " as StornoEntry <<start>>
state "  " as End <<end>>

[*] --> DRAFT : new invoice
DRAFT --> IN_REVIEW
' [norank]: the return edge must not influence the left-to-right rank order,
' otherwise Graphviz may put IN_REVIEW left of DRAFT when it breaks the cycle.
IN_REVIEW -[norank]-> DRAFT
IN_REVIEW --> ISSUED : e-invoice generated\nsuccessfully
note on link
  Not a direct action: "Senden" requests a SEND-triggered
  e-invoice generation job (GenerationJobResultHandler.resolveSendOutcome);
  the invoice stays IN_REVIEW until that job completes and
  validation resolves VALID. See Runtime View, "Send an Invoice".
  A VALID-tooling-UNAVAILABLE result can still be forced through
  with an audited override reason (finalize-override) — the one
  case this edge remains a direct, synchronous action.
end note
ISSUED --> End : stays sent

DRAFT -down-> VOIDED
IN_REVIEW -down-> VOIDED
ISSUED -down-> CANCELLED : storno
note top of CANCELLED
  Original invoice is tagged
  CANCELLED on storno and stays so;
  the storno document is a
  separate invoice (type code 384)
  created in CANCELLED via
  Invoice.withInitialStatus(CANCELLED)
  (ADR-025) — status has a private
  setter, so this factory is the
  construction-time-only door
  around it, deliberately outside
  InvoiceStateMachine's own edge
  table (no prior status to check).
end note

StornoEntry -down-> CANCELLED : storno document is\ncreated directly\nin CANCELLED

VOIDED -down-> End
CANCELLED -down-> End

legend right
  |= Status |= Color |
  |DRAFT|<back:#5F6368><color:#FFFFFF> editable </color></back>|
  |IN_REVIEW|<back:#C34118><color:#FFFFFF> awaiting review </color></back>|
  |ISSUED|<back:#1A73E8><color:#FFFFFF> read-only; final unless cancelled </color></back>|
  |CANCELLED|<back:#455A64><color:#FFFFFF> terminal: storno </color></back>|
  |VOIDED|<back:#D93025><color:#FFFFFF> terminal: discarded unsent </color></back>|
endlegend

@enduml
